WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.240
Open the branch selector. Choose the branch that contains the prepared Training Echo module.

2
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:34.354
This is the original training branch. These prepared files are the starting point for the release.

3
00:00:34.354 --> 00:00:50.479
Open modules, then training_echo. Each module has its own folder.

4
00:00:50.479 --> 00:00:58.482
The folder contains the manifest, implementation, dependencies, fixture and output assertion.

5
00:00:58.482 --> 00:01:06.563
From the module folder, open manifest.yaml.

6
00:01:06.563 --> 00:01:42.055
The manifest declares the input, output and runtime. This prepared version starts disabled and hidden.

7
00:01:42.055 --> 00:01:50.057
From the module folder, open run.py.

8
00:01:50.057 --> 00:02:25.773
run.py reads the input text and writes training_echo.csv with the text and its character count.

9
00:02:25.773 --> 00:02:33.770
From the module folder, open requirements.txt.

10
00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:50.668
requirements.txt is empty: this training module uses only the Python standard library.

11
00:02:50.668 --> 00:02:58.703
From the module folder, open validation.json.

12
00:02:58.703 --> 00:03:15.628
validation.json supplies a known input and an invalid case for local acceptance.

13
00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:23.635
From the module folder, open assert_output.py.

14
00:03:23.635 --> 00:03:59.324
assert_output.py checks the actual CSV contents, including escaping and the character count.

15
00:03:59.324 --> 00:04:12.333
Return to the module folder. Next, validate these files before reviewing the pull request.

16
00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:27.600
Run the module acceptance command against the prepared files.

17
00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:42.867
A passing result checks the output CSV contents, escaping and character count.

18
00:04:42.867 --> 00:05:13.007
From the repository, open Pull requests. The completed demonstration PRs are in Closed.

19
00:05:13.007 --> 00:05:25.236
Open PR #54. Read the description and source branch, then inspect the changed files.

20
00:05:25.236 --> 00:06:20.825
Review the module implementation, manifest and acceptance files before release.

21
00:06:20.825 --> 00:06:49.726
Read the changed lines, then return to the conversation to inspect checks and the merge record.

22
00:06:49.726 --> 00:07:26.719
Inspect the completed checks for this PR before relying on the merge.

23
00:07:26.719 --> 00:07:39.667
Next, watch the recorded release and verify that its outcome matches this reviewed change.

24
00:07:39.667 --> 00:08:00.690
Open Checks, then expand module-ci to see its individual jobs.

25
00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:10.572
Select validate to open the recorded job and its conclusion.

26
00:08:10.572 --> 00:08:42.667
Inspect the validation result and its logged steps for this exact PR head.

27
00:08:42.667 --> 00:09:00.300
Original recording: review the passing checks, then merge the prepared module PR.

28
00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:17.933
The initial released manifest is disabled and hidden.

29
00:09:17.933 --> 00:09:25.167
Original registry readback: locate the released module and inspect its flags.

30
00:09:25.167 --> 00:09:32.400
Both Training Echo and Coptis are held disabled and hidden here.

31
00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:48.523
Start in the training branch. Backend access rules live outside the module folder.

32
00:09:48.523 --> 00:10:03.762
Open supabase, then functions, then _shared.

33
00:10:03.762 --> 00:10:13.839
Open module-entitlements.ts to find the module-to-tier policy.

34
00:10:13.839 --> 00:10:37.943
MODULE_ACCESS assigns each module its minimum account tier. Training Echo begins at Silver.

35
00:10:37.943 --> 00:10:52.800
A tier change requires deployment of submit-job. The manifest release updates the registry separately.

36
00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:59.800
Original deployment: release the reviewed Silver policy through submit-job.

37
00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:06.800
Registry synchronization and function deployment are separate release steps.

38
00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:18.300
The earlier frontend publication attempt was blocked.

39
00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:29.800
The following verification explains why publication was unnecessary for this release.

40
00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:39.900
The published Skill Catalog reads the registry to discover modules.

41
00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:50.000
The live frontend already supported this release; no frontend publication was needed.

42
00:11:50.000 --> 00:12:20.134
From the repository, open Pull requests. The completed demonstration PRs are in Closed.

43
00:12:20.134 --> 00:12:32.154
Open PR #56. Read the description and source branch, then inspect the changed files.

44
00:12:32.154 --> 00:12:57.119
enabled allows new jobs. ui.visible controls whether the catalog offers the module.

45
00:12:57.119 --> 00:13:14.052
Read the changed lines, then return to the conversation to inspect checks and the merge record.

46
00:13:14.052 --> 00:13:51.110
Inspect the completed checks for this PR before relying on the merge.

47
00:13:51.110 --> 00:14:04.200
Next, watch the recorded release and verify that its outcome matches this reviewed change.

48
00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:12.500
Original recorded change: enable the module and make it visible through PR #56.

49
00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:20.800
The reviewed manifest is now ready for its registry release.

50
00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:42.300
Original recording: merge PR #56 after its checks pass.

51
00:14:42.300 --> 00:15:03.800
Verify that the registry workflow checked out the intended merge commit.

52
00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:29.933
From the repository, open Actions to inspect the automatic registry release.

53
00:15:29.933 --> 00:15:43.034
Choose the run for the intended merge. Its commit must match the change you meant to release.

54
00:15:43.034 --> 00:16:12.933
This completed run projects the manifest into the registry. It does not deploy frontend or function code.

55
00:16:12.933 --> 00:16:19.933
Original Silver test: Training Echo is enabled and visible in the catalog.

56
00:16:19.933 --> 00:16:25.933
Enter the test text and select Run. The following submission is the original recorded action.

57
00:16:25.933 --> 00:16:47.933
The accepted job is queued and executed. Wait for its status to change.

58
00:16:47.933 --> 00:16:52.933
The job has succeeded and its result is available.

59
00:16:52.933 --> 00:17:04.800
The verified private CSV contains the exact input text and its character count.

60
00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:35.173
From the repository, open Pull requests. The completed demonstration PRs are in Closed.

61
00:17:35.173 --> 00:17:47.181
Open PR #57. Read the description and source branch, then inspect the changed files.

62
00:17:47.181 --> 00:18:12.173
This change updates the title and description, then removes the module from catalog discovery.

63
00:18:12.173 --> 00:18:29.113
Read the changed lines, then return to the conversation to inspect checks and the merge record.

64
00:18:29.113 --> 00:19:06.212
Inspect the completed checks for this PR before relying on the merge.

65
00:19:06.212 --> 00:19:19.333
Next, watch the recorded release and verify that its outcome matches this reviewed change.

66
00:19:19.333 --> 00:19:27.300
Original recorded change: update the title and description, then hide catalog discovery.

67
00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:35.267
These manifest fields are released through PR #57.

68
00:19:35.267 --> 00:19:57.433
Original recording: merge PR #57 and verify its registry release.

69
00:19:57.433 --> 00:20:19.600
This metadata and visibility change needs no separate backend deployment.

70
00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:29.600
Original readback: the module is no longer offered in the catalog.

71
00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:39.600
Hiding discovery preserves previously created jobs and their results.

72
00:20:39.600 --> 00:21:09.610
From the repository, open Pull requests. The completed demonstration PRs are in Closed.

73
00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:21.642
Open PR #58. Read the description and source branch, then inspect the changed files.

74
00:21:21.642 --> 00:22:16.636
The access policy changes from Silver to Gold. The manifest separately restores catalog visibility.

75
00:22:16.636 --> 00:22:33.619
Read the changed lines, then return to the conversation to inspect checks and the merge record.

76
00:22:33.619 --> 00:23:10.944
Inspect the completed checks for this PR before relying on the merge.

77
00:23:10.944 --> 00:23:23.800
Next, watch the recorded release and verify that its outcome matches this reviewed change.

78
00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:33.033
Original recorded change: raise the minimum tier from Silver to Gold.

79
00:23:33.033 --> 00:23:42.267
PR #58 also restores catalog visibility; these are separate controls.

80
00:23:42.267 --> 00:24:04.233
Original recording: merge PR #58 after review and passing checks.

81
00:24:04.233 --> 00:24:26.200
Registry synchronization reveals the module. The new tier rule still needs function deployment.

82
00:24:26.200 --> 00:24:33.933
